    "updated_at": "2019-08-28T19:52:32Z",
    "body": "#168 was a pretty massive merge that did a lot of reorganization--it's entirely possible that it broke something.\r\n\r\nThe whole reason we made the changes in #168 was because the previous init system couldn't tell you where the errors were coming from, and after that merge we've usually see errors pointing to specific lines. I find it a little odd that your shell is complaining about things from the very first line of the sourced script--suggests that the error probably isn't where I think it is.\r\n\r\nIf I could ask a favor, would you mind posting the contents of your `config.fish` up to the point where you initialize starship? If you can't due to privacy reasons, that's fine, it'll just make this a little harder to debug.\r\n\r\nAs for the immediate bug, does replacing `starship init fish | source` with `source (starship init fish --print-full-init | psub)` cause the shell to do anything differently?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/starship/starship/issues/comments/525896914/reactions",
