    "updated_at": "2019-08-29T08:28:54Z",
    "body": "@chipbuster Thanks for suggestions.\r\n\r\nI was able to figure out what went wrong. I had overridden `cat(1)` with [`bat`](https://github.com/sharkdp/bat) which is kind of nicer version of the command. Seems like Starship tried to use that in some point and capture its output as is causing the error. Would make sense with error being about unexpected string end.\r\n\r\nI've removed that dumb alias now and it's working perfectly. Generally, it might be a good idea to prefix calls to system commands with `command` (eg. `command cat`) so user-defined aliases and functions will be discarded. See: https://fishshell.com/docs/current/commands.html#command\r\n\r\nI'm no Rust expert but I might be able to take a look at this later on if desired.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
