    "body": "@nikoheikkila Glad you found it!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I still can't reproduce that error on my end:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/63960843-407c8500-ca44-11e9-98c6-39cadb93a711.png)\r\n\r\nIt's also curious that this is causing an issue, because as far as I know, starship doesn't execute anything within a shell environment--all our external calls should be passed through `std::process::Command`, which runs in a non-shell environment and shouldn't see any aliases.\r\n\r\nIn fact, the only shell script for the fish init is what you posted in the first post (the `fish_prompt` function).\r\n\r\nIf you still want to have a look, let me know and I can give you some pointers on the overall code structure!",
