    "body": "@nikoheikkila Thanks for the snippet. I was able to reproduce it and...it seems like either a bug in fish or a problem with us not understanding the guarantees offered by the shell.\r\n\r\nIt looks like using `psub` actually causes `fish` to use the `cat` command: [source code](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/blob/master/share/functions/psub.fish#L42)\r\n\r\nAnd the result:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/64028691-f05efa80-caf7-11e9-8525-ff4c45da99b6.png)\r\n\r\nDo you think that looks like a bug in the `fish` implementation of `psub`? Or is there something we should be doing in starship to work around that?\r\n",
