    "created_at": "2019-08-30T19:31:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-30T19:31:43Z",
    "body": "The `psub` implementation should ensure it's running the correct version of `cat` by adding `set -l cat (command -v cat)` before calling it and referencing it via `$cat`. You can verify it fixes the issue by saving a modified version to `~/.config/fish/functions/psub.fish`. Then again, every command there should potentially be safeguarded including `echo`…\r\n\r\nMaybe the best solution would have Fish functions support a _flag_ which would prevent running aliased commands but that would require much discussion on Fish development part.\r\n\r\nCould Starship assert during a command call that when something like `cat` is being invoked it refers exactly to `/bin/cat` and nothing else? I'm not sure if the location of `cat` changes between different systems so that might hurt cross-platform compatibility at some point – unless there's a way to dynamically query full path to command.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
