    "created_at": "2019-08-30T22:01:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-30T22:01:29Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately, I don't think we can make that assertion, simply because we aim to be cross-platform (we currently have packages out for Windows, MacOS, Linux, and Android) and I don't think `/bin/cat` exists on all of those. \r\n\r\nI think most shells provide a way to determine if something is an alias, but I don't know what other programs/builtins are being called by the init script at the moment...\r\n\r\nI don't see a great way to fix this on the technological side in Starship at the moment. @matchai Perhaps we could open an issue against fish and see if they'd be willing to fix this for us?",
